# ============================================================================
# Build-context ignore file — this is the deploy safety boundary
# ============================================================================
# Railway's builder (Nixpacks, and Railpack after it) reads this exact filename.
# Railpack's own documentation states that when no `.dockerignore` exists in the
# project root, *every* file in the directory is included in the build context.
# `railway up` uploads the directory it is run from, so this file is the only
# thing standing between a laptop working copy and a shipped image:
#
#   AllinOne/.env holds real credentials (Atlas URI with a password, Upstash
#   Redis URI, JWT secrets, ENCRYPTION_KEY, an SMTP app password). It is
#   untracked, so a GitHub-connected deploy never sees it — but a CLI deploy
#   ships whatever this file fails to name.
#
# Two facts to keep straight when editing this:
#   * `.env.example` is deliberately NOT ignored. Nixpacks may want a sample env
#     file present, and it contains only placeholder values. The pattern below
#     matches `.env` and its variants and then re-includes the example.
#   * `scripts/` holds `worker-preflight.js`, which `npm run start:worker` executes
#     inside the image. Ignoring the whole directory would make the worker service
#     crash on boot, so the directory is ignored with that one file re-included.
#
# prisma/ is NOT ignored as a directory: `postinstall` runs `prisma generate`,
# which needs `prisma/schema.prisma`. Only the seeding entry point is excluded —
# it can write to a production database and has no business in a runtime image.

# --- Secrets and local environment -------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
.run/secrets/

# --- Dependencies and build output (regenerated by the build) ----------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Sources that must not reach a runtime image -----------------------------
test/
docs/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
tmp/
temp/
.backup/

# --- Operational scripts, except the one the worker boot guard needs ---------
scripts/*
!scripts/worker-preflight.js

# --- Seed data: writes to whatever DATABASE_URL points at --------------------
prisma/seed.ts

# --- Local tooling / VCS ------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# --- Monitoring stacks that are dev-only and are not started by this image ---
infrastructure/
